      "diff": "@@ -26,17 +26,84 @@ It is used for troubleshooting, analysis, development and education.\n \n === Bug Fixes\n \n-// The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n+The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-// * wssalink:2021-07[]\n-// Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n-// wsbuglink:xxxxx[].\n+* wssalink:2021-07[]\n+Bluetooth DHT dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:17651[].\n // cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: xxxxx\n-// Fixed in release-3.4: xxxxx\n-// Fixed in master-3.2: xxxxx\n+// Fixed in master: ed98abe2\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 1ffe0cef\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: 4cd492c1\n+// Fixed in master-3.2: 98056d8f\n // CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n-// CWE-762: Mismatched Memory Management Routines\n+// CWE-674: Uncontrolled Recursion\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-09[]\n+Bluetooth SDP dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:17635[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: e15e9874\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 492a7038\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: b18691c5\n+// Fixed in master-3.2: ae45fcd6\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-10[]\n+Bluetooth DHT dissector large loop.\n+wsbuglink:17677[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: 79a9fe1c\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: e138ec5d\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: d3c762dc\n+// Fixed in master-3.2: 2f017bb7\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-834: Excessive Iteration\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-11[]\n+PNRP dissector large loop.\n+wsbuglink:17684[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: 9104a374\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: f21b9447\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: d6d15b97\n+// Fixed in master-3.2: 81b5d29c\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-834: Excessive Iteration\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-12[]\n+C12.22 dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:17636[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: b760c356\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 1b9972ae\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: 7ac1d5be\n+// Fixed in master-3.2: 9a1ef88c\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-13[]\n+IEEE 802.11 dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:17704[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: 0b473c01\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: ab3bb461\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: 00581507\n+// Fixed in master-3.2: 8f6d0c79\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-14[]\n+Modbus dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:17703[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: bb41b661\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: e1efbe23\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: 55c12cc7\n+// Fixed in master-3.2: 9e453dd5\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference\n \n The following bugs have been fixed:\n \n@@ -46,6 +113,18 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* Wireshark is solely responsible for the decline of shopping malls in your area.\n // cp /dev/null /tmp/buglist.txt ; for bugnumber in `git log v3.2.10rc0.. | gsed -e 's/\\(close\\|fix\\|resolv\\)[^ ]* #/\\nclose #/gI' | grep ^close | sed -e 's/close.*#\\([1-9][0-9]*\\).*/\\1/' | sort -V -u` ; do \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/tools/gen-bugnote\" $bugnumber; pbpaste >> /tmp/buglist.txt; done\n \n+* Allow for '\\0' (NULL) character as filter instead of requiring 0x00 for the character match wsbuglink:16525[].\n+\n+* Dumpcap with threads reports double received count vs captured wsbuglink:17089[].\n+\n+* I/O Graphs values reset to default with 3.5 due to change of UAT wsbuglink:17623[].\n+\n+* TShark stops capturing when capturing with multiple files and packet printing enabled wsbuglink:17654[].\n+\n+* Wireshark is unable to decode the IMSI IE received in BSSMAP Perform Location request wsbuglink:17667[].\n+\n+* Crash in flow analysis for TCP wsbuglink:17722[].\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n There are no new features in this release.\n@@ -67,8 +146,21 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n === Updated Protocol Support\n \n // Add one protocol per line between the -- delimiters.\n+// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.2.17.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+BT-DHT\n+BT SDP\n+C12.22\n+CAN FD\n+CSN1\n+EAPOL-MKA\n+EVS\n+GSM BSSMAP LE\n+IEEE 802.11\n+PNRP\n+TCP\n+TLS\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n",
